faq:[['Which operating systems are supported?','DevWorkspace is a Windows x64 desktop application. It can recognize projects targeting other platforms; the application itself runs on Windows.'],['Do I need the .NET SDK to get started?','The installer and portable packages include their runtime. Building and running your own projects requires their SDKs and package managers. Developing DevWorkspace from source requires the .NET 10 SDK and access to DevExpress WPF packages.'],['Does it replace my IDE or terminal?','DevWorkspace brings projects, Git context and everyday operations together. It works alongside your existing IDE, terminal, Git, SDKs and project tools.'],['How are updates applied?','The installed version downloads updates in the background. Ready updates apply on the next launch or when you choose Restart now. All releases are available on GitHub Releases.'],['Can a team use it?','Launch profiles and workspace configurations can be shared. Team configuration in the development hub carries relative project paths and required tools. Commands are reviewed before importing on another computer.'],['What are the license terms?','Original project code is MIT licensed. DevExpress is a commercial dependency; it and other third-party components retain their own terms. See the license and third-party notices linked in the footer.']]
